1
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:23,760
What are you doing?

2
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:25,480
Why don’t you have breakfast before leaving?

3
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:26,800
I’m not hungry.

4
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:28,800
Um...

5
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:31,360
I looked into it yesterday,

6
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:32,680
the laws and culture of your planet.

7
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:34,800
It’s true, I was wrong.

8
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:36,520
I apologize to you.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,479
Keep a one-meter distance from me.

10
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:42,280
Being angry will affect your magnetic field,

11
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,400
and bring you bad luck.

12
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:44,400
Annoying.

13
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:57,120
You’re here so early.

14
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:00,240
Isn’t this the normal time?

15
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:01,480
I was being sarcastic.

16
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:02,960
The meeting’s almost over, and now you show up.

17
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:03,960
Meeting?

18
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:05,400
What meeting?

19
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:06,840
Didn’t you schedule a meeting with Mr. Qin, the investor, today?

20
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:07,960
We agreed to meet.

21
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:11,160
But didn’t Mr. Jiang say the meeting was this afternoon?

22
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:12,560
When was it moved to the morning?

23
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:13,440
I don’t know.

24
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:15,120
Anyway, it started over an hour ago.

25
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,240
Mr. Qin, don’t worry.

26
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:20,840
We’ll make sure to improve everything according to your requests.

27
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:24,080
I trust Mr. Jiang to handle things well.

28
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:26,200
Where’s that young lady from last time?

29
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:27,480
Her?

30
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:28,840
She’s probably late.

31
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:30,920
Young people these days are always like that.

32
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,320
I’ll make sure to have a word with her later.

33
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:34,200
Alright then.

34
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:36,160
Let’s follow up in a couple of days.

35
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:36,640
Alright.

36
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:37,680
Sure, Mr. Qin.

37
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:39,040
Here’s the revised plan for 'Sweet Strike.'

38
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:42,480
Oh, I’m sorry, Mr. Qin.

39
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,160
What are you doing?

40
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:45,560
I’m so sorry.

41
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,200
The meeting’s already finished.

42
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,720
What’s the point of bringing this now?

43
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:49,840
What’s the use?

44
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:52,960
Mr. Qin,

45
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,120
please don’t be upset.

46
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:56,040
I instructed my assistant to inform her earlier.

47
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:57,440
Maybe the assistant forgot.

48
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,280
Anyway, that's my fault at work.

49
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,440
Please don't blame Qi Miao.

50
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:02,480
Qi Miao, is it?

51
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,720
You should learn from your teacher Jiang.

52
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:07,360
Punctuality is the most important thing for young people.

53
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:08,880
I'll head out now.

54
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,120
Take care, Mr. Qin.

55
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:11,960
I'm really sorry, Mr. Qin.

56
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,160
I promise this won't happen again.

57
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:15,200
Teacher Jiang.

58
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,120
I really didn’t receive any message.

59
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,920
About the meeting time change.

60
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:20,080
Maybe the assistant forgot.

61
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:23,280
Well...

62
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:24,880
What about my revised proposal?

63
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:25,400
Leave it there.

64
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:26,560
I'll pass it to Mr. Qin later.

65
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,600
If there's nothing else, please head out.

66
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,320
Sister Jianjian.

67
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:42,480
Sister Jianjian.

68
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:45,600
Where is Sister Jianjian?

69
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,640
She went to a concert today.

70
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,520
I'm watching the shop for her.

71
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:52,760
Are you her new assistant?

72
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,240
You look quite handsome.

73
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,160
By the way,

74
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:57,000
Do you need anything from Jianjian?

75
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:58,000
No, nothing.

76
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:00,400
I just wanted to ask how the jade is selling.

77
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:01,280
Alright then.

78
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:01,800
I'll come back tomorrow.

79
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:03,440
Hold on.

80
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,160
Have a seat.

81
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:05,400
What's the matter?

82
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:06,120
Sit down.

83
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:11,720
Here's the thing.

84
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:12,520
A couple of days ago,

85
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:14,000
A jewelry dealer came to the shop.

86
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,960
He said he was very interested in your jade.

87
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:17,000
Really?

88
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:20,840
And that dealer is quite generous.

89
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,840
He said he wants to buy all of your jade.

90
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:24,120
That's fantastic!

91
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,720
I knew it, I knew this time I'd make money!

92
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:26,600
Where is he?

93
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,280
I'll go find him.

94
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:27,880
Wait a second.

95
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,240
Now, here's the thing.

96
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:31,960
What is it?

97
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:35,120
The boss is planning to hold a jewelry exhibition soon.

98
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:38,120
You can always supply those jades and such.

99
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:39,680
But the issue is...

100
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:42,360
Right now, he wants to find a unique crystal.

101
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,600
He's searching everywhere for it.

102
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:45,320
Do you happen to have one?

103
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:46,560
Maybe?

104
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,760
A crystal.

105
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:52,080
Something like this.

106
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,640
This crystal looks so familiar.

107
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:04,000
Oh, right!

108
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:06,000
I have a crystal just like this at home.

109
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:07,880
Really?

110
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:09,280
What a coincidence!

111
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:13,000
But the thing is, this crystal isn't mine.

112
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:15,400
I'm pretty sure Brother Ruichi wouldn't want to sell it.

113
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:16,600
Actually, about that...

114
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:17,640
Selling isn't necessary.

115
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:18,600
The boss said...

116
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:19,720
As long as you're willing to rent it to him.

117
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:21,000
Just for a two-day exhibition, that's all.

118
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:23,800
And he’s offering a very generous price!

119
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:24,760
How much?

120
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,280
Five thousand?

121
00:04:26,439 --> 00:04:27,200
Five hundred thousand.

122
00:04:27,439 --> 00:04:27,920
Five...

123
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:30,600
Five hundred thousand?!

124
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:31,960
Is that for real?

125
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,000
He’s already put down a deposit.

126
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,320
Once the deal is done...

127
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:40,440
Not only will you get these gold leaves...

128
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:43,240
You’ll also receive the remaining five hundred thousand as a rental fee.

129
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:43,960
So, what do you think?

130
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:44,640
Not a bad deal, right?

131
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:45,800
Not bad, not bad at all.

132
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,400
I'll go talk to Brother Ruichi right now.

133
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,040
Hold on a second.

134
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:49,560
I’m not done yet.

135
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:50,440
Oh, please go on.

136
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:52,280
Here’s what I think.

137
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,200
With such a great opportunity...

138
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:56,600
Why do you feel the need to consult your friend?

139
00:04:58,240 --> 00:04:59,320
And besides, they said...

140
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:01,240
It's just for one or two days.

141
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:04,840
Wouldn't it be better to keep all that money for yourself?

142
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:06,640
Sounds like it makes sense.

143
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,200
Don't worry.

144
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,520
I know exactly how to handle this.

145
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:12,160
I, Qi Dongdong, stand for just two words:

146
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:13,120
Reliability.

147
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:14,960
I promise to get you the crystal.

148
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,760
Well then, here's to a happy collaboration.

149
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,400
Happy collaboration, happy collaboration.

150
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:26,040
Richi bro!

151
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:28,560
Richi bro!

152
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:32,160
Bro!

153
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:32,840
What's wrong?

154
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:33,880
Don't scare me like this.

155
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:35,040
I'm fine.

156
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:39,400
If you're fine, then why this gloomy vibe?

157
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,600
It's kind of creepy.

158
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:43,680
I just want some peace and quiet.

159
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:44,960
Bro.

160
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:47,680
Did you and my sister have a fight?

161
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:48,880
No.

162
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:52,920
I just made your sister upset.

163
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:55,000
Bro.

164
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,280
You are such a good man.

165
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:57,560
With that kind of awareness,

166
00:05:57,640 --> 00:05:58,440
I'll help you.

167
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:02,880
How are you going to help me?

168
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:05,360
Well,

169
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,640
I remember you have a blue crystal.

170
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:12,280
Actually, my sister really likes things like crystals.

171
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,040
If you give her the crystal,

172
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:15,320
she'll definitely be happy.

173
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:17,440
No way.

174
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,040
Energy crystals are off-limits.

175
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:20,040
Think of another way.

176
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,360
Looks like borrowing the crystal is out of the question.

177
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:22,560
I'll have to think of another plan.

178
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:26,200
It's just that gifting a crystal is the easiest solution.

179
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:28,640
Anything else would be way too complicated.

180
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,440
As long as it works,

181
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:30,360
the process doesn't matter.

182
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:34,280
Alright then.

183
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:40,720
You're sure this will work?

184
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,000
Relax.

185
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,240
From my over 20 years

186
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:44,320
of experience making my sister angry,

187
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:45,320
if you use this trick,

188
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,240
it will absolutely work.

189
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:51,480
Alright, I'll listen to you.

190
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,200
Bro.

191
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:55,080
Can we take it easy next time?

192
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:57,480
No problem.

193
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,440
Qi Miao, why aren't you here yet?

194
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,160
Alan's concert is about to start.

195
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:06,000
Hurry up!

196
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:07,240
I just got off work.

197
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,080
I'm on my way!

198
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:09,480
Qi Miao.

199
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,480
President Qin is coming over for a meeting tomorrow morning.

200
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:15,160
Stay late and revise the new script.

201
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,360
But it's already seven o'clock.

202
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,560
If I start now,

203
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,520
how long will it take to finish?

204
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:23,800
President Qin really thinks highly of you right now.

205
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:26,160
You wouldn’t want to waste this opportunity, would you?

206
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:29,320
But I...

207
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:30,600
Just hang in there for a bit.

208
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,000
At the next meeting,

209
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,400
I'll give you lots of praise in front of President Qin.

210
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:41,480
Of course.

211
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,280
Qi Miao.

212
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:43,400
You just don't deserve,

213
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:45,080
any happiness at all.

214
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:00,560
This song,

215
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,000
is dedicated to,

216
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,200
you who fearlessly chase your dreams.

217
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:18,200
Even though you missed the concert,

218
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:20,920
happiness will always be with you.

219
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,640
May your dreams always burn bright.

220
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:27,560
I will.

221
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:29,160
You must be hungry.

222
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:30,440
I made some food.

223
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:44,280
You made all of this?

224
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:45,120
That's right.

225
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:46,200
I followed some tutorials.

226
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:46,920
It was pretty simple.

227
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:49,320
Qi Miao.

228
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,080
About what happened yesterday...

229
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:52,200
I'm sorry.

230
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,320
Since you helped me fulfill,

231
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,800
my dream of watching Alan's concert,

232
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:57,520
and even prepared such a feast for me,

233
00:09:57,880 --> 00:09:58,840
I forgive you.

234
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:01,920
By the way,

235
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:03,760
you mentioned before that kissing me

236
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:05,560
was to replenish the crystal energy.

237
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:08,240
So why am I able to help you recharge your energy?

238
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,200
I’ve mentioned before,

239
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:11,760
we Lancans

240
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,240
can see other people's magnetic fields.

241
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,960
If we spend time with someone who shares the same magnetic field,

242
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,160
we can replenish each other's energy.

243
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:20,200
What if you meet

244
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,040
a lot of people with the same type of magnetic field at the same time?

245
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:24,120
On our Lanca planet, there's a vow,

246
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,400
if you meet someone with a matching magnetic field

247
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:27,440
and establish a bond,

248
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:29,120
you must stay together for life,

249
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:30,520
until death.

250
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:32,200
Establish a bond?

251
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:34,040
Yes, establish a bond.

252
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:37,880
It's what you Earthlings call marriage.

253
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:41,800
And the bonding process is the equivalent of your wedding night.

254
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:42,520
Men and women...

255
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:43,240
Stop, stop, stop!

256
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:45,400
If you keep going, it’s going to get inappropriate for kids!

257
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,440
But,

258
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:49,880
once bonded,

259
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:51,920
you must stay together forever.

260
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:54,760
Your planet is quite romantic, huh?

261
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:57,360
Isn't it the same on your planet?

262
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:00,840
If only it were like that.

263
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:04,400
Human emotions are incredibly complicated.

264
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:06,880
Forget it,

265
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,960
even if I explain it, you wouldn’t understand.

266
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:10,080
Here, drink.

267
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:24,520
Why is this drink so bitter?

268
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:27,440
You just don’t get it, do you?

269
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,040
Alcohol, despite tasting bitter,

270
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:33,040
can help you temporarily forget the things that make you sad.

271
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:34,840
Drink a bit more, and you’ll see.

272
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:35,440
Come on.

273
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,040
Another!

274
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:40,880
Alright!

275
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:42,360
As long as you’re happy.

276
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:24,880
Brother Ruichi.

277
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:26,280
Brother Ruichi.

278
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:41,360
Bro.

279
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:43,680
This is all the help I can give you.

280
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:44,440
Take this,

281
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,160
consider it a token of gratitude.
